CM_ BO_ 2 "Steering angle sensor. Our testing confirmed steering-angle behavior, steering-rate behavior, fixed 0x07 field, approximately 100 Hz transmission, and 4-bit rolling counter.";
CM_ BO_ 361 "Nissan LKAS steering-control message. NOT seen in any of our captures - we have not confirmed this car transmits it, or on which bus. LKAS_BUS in manual_nissancan.py is a placeholder until we capture it.";
CM_ BO_ 634 "Observed turn-signal state message. Captured on BUS 2 at 47.5 Hz over 50432 frames. REPORTS lamp state rather than commanding it: byte 4 toggles with the physical flash at about 1.43 Hz, and every sustained hazard period begins 20-30 ms AFTER a 0x3AF pulse. Transmitting this message is not expected to command the lamps.";
CM_ SG_ 634 SET_0x4D "Constant 0x4D across all 50432 captured frames. Observed on received frames; not validated for transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 634 COUNTER_27A "Confirmed 4-bit rolling counter in byte 6 low nibble. Sequence 0 through 15 then wraps to 0.";
CM_ SG_ 634 CHECKSUM_27A "Confirmed additive checksum. Checksum = (Byte1 + Byte2 + Byte3 + Byte4 + Byte5 + Byte6 + 0x7C) & 0xFF.";
CM_ BO_ 943 "Observed hazard-switch press message. Captured on BUS 0 at 10.1 Hz; bytes 2-8 constant 0x00, no counter and no checksum. 110 pulses observed, width 0.131 s min / 0.250 s median / 0.560 s max, so a press is roughly 2-3 frames at 10 Hz. This is a hazard switch input indication; all 35 sustained hazard periods in 0x27A began 20-30 ms after a pulse here.";
CM_ BO_ 1549 "Door-status message also contains turn-signal state. Captured on BUS 0 at 10.3 Hz. Byte 2 toggles 0x06 <-> 0x66 in lockstep with the 0x27A flash, which confirms bits 5 and 6 as the two blinker lamps. Like 0x27A this message REPORTS lamp state.";


CM_ BO_ 451 "Factory ProPILOT braking associated with this message in 2025 Leaf road test. Existing BRAKE_PRESSURE and BRAKE_ACTIVE names preserved. Control request versus feedback unknown. Decode only.";
CM_ SG_ 451 BRAKE_PRESSURE "Raw magnitude 0-364 observed, not calibrated to pressure units. Original name preserved.";
CM_ SG_ 451 BRAKE_ACTIVE "Observed during automatic braking. Cannot infer this bit actuates brakes.";
CM_ SG_ 451 BRAKING_STATUS "Additional braking-related status observed at Byte 6 bit 2; detailed meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 451 BRAKE_COUNTER "Byte 6 bits 0-1, observed cycling 0,1,2,3.";
CM_ SG_ 451 BRAKE_CHECKSUM "Byte 8 additive integrity relation confirmed in 263475 captured frames; receive-side only.";
CM_ BO_ 460 "Original BRAKE_PEDAL name retained. Actual captured message length 4 bytes, not 8. Its magnitude changes during automatic braking too, so does not exclusively indicate driver pedal input.";
CM_ BO_ 459 "Additional candidate received message 0x1CB. Status correlated with automatic braking; raw value associated with manual braking. Exact meanings unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 459 BRAKE_RELATED_STATUS "Byte 2 bit 5; active in 81.8 percent of braking intervals vs 4.5 percent inactive intervals in sampled comparison. Not an actuation command.";
CM_ SG_ 459 BRAKE_RELATED_VALUE "Byte 3 raw value; associated with manual brake testing, units and function unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 654 "Additional status candidate 0x28E; observed on Panda bus 1; association with factory braking, not a verified command.";
CM_ BO_ 682 "Additional brake-related message 0x2AA. Correlated with factory braking, exact field definitions and ECU source unverified.";
CM_ BO_ 688 "Additional status candidate 0x2B0 observed on Panda bus 1 during factory braking.";
CM_ BO_ 761 "Additional status candidate 0x2F9. Its observed bit mostly clears while factory braking is active; not a verified brake command.";
CM_ BO_ 861 "Message 0x35D contains a status candidate correlated with manual brake input; exact function unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 634 BRAKE_RELATED_STATUS "Observed correlation with brake-pedal activity at Byte 4 bit 5. This message also reports turn signal state; does not control brakes.";
CM_ SG_ 852 BRAKE_RELATED_STATUS "Observed correlation with manual brake input; exact meaning unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 861 BRAKE_RELATED_STATUS "Observed correlation with manual brake input; exact meaning unverified.";
CM_ BO_ 1354 "HVAC message 0x54A recorded on buses 0 and 2 at around 10Hz. Names mostly preserved from ZE1 DBC. No conventional rolling counter or payload checksum confirmed. Receive-side only.";
CM_ SG_ 1354 CCStatusPlusUnknown "Byte 1 alternates 0x3C and 0xDA, exact purpose not established.";
CM_ SG_ 1354 Unknown_54A_3_BIT0 "Byte 4 bit 0 changes during HVAC operation, purpose unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 1354 Unknown_54A_3_BIT2 "Byte 4 bit 2, inverted HVAC ON/OFF association: 0 observed during ON, 1 during OFF. This is NOT verified as AC compressor power.";
CM_ SG_ 1354 ClimateControlSetpoint "Byte 5 increments with selected temperature changes: observed raw 78-84, 0 when inactive. Exact display scaling not independently confirmed.";
CM_ SG_ 1354 AmbientTempAC "Original ZE1 name retained; byte 8 constant 0x6D in newer recording; physical scaling not verified.";

CM_ BO_ 372 "Observed gear-position status on Panda buses 0 and 2, DLC 8 at approx 100 Hz, during stationary P/R/D shifting. Receive-side observation; no command behavior verified.";
CM_ SG_ 372 GEAR_POSITION "Byte 4 complete code: 0xAA Park, 0x99 Reverse, 0xBB Drive. Correlated with driver's gear-selection sequence; this is not evidence of an accepted shift request.";
CM_ SG_ 372 GEAR_COUNTER "Byte 5 lower nibble cycles 0..15; one discontinuity among 28334 consecutive captured bus-0 transitions. Other bits not decoded.";
CM_ BO_ 976 "Observed gear-system status on Panda buses 0 and 2, DLC 6 at approx 50 Hz. Byte 2 encodes gear-correlated states, including a delayed secondary Reverse state. Receive-side only.";
CM_ SG_ 976 GEAR_STATE "Observed Byte 2: 0x83 Park, 0x85 initial Reverse, 0xC5 sustained Reverse, 0x89 Drive, 0x81 transition. These are correlations, not verified shift commands.";
CM_ SG_ 976 GEAR_COUNTER "Byte 6 bits 0-1 cycle modulo 4, with some discontinuities. Remaining bits of Byte 6 are not established as a checksum.";
CM_ BO_ 1402 "Observed reverse-associated status on Panda buses 0 and 2, DLC 8 at approx 10 Hz. Changes after Reverse selection. Not a confirmed shifter request, reversing-light or camera control.";
CM_ SG_ 1402 REVERSE_RELATED_STATE "Byte 1 usually 0x08 outside Reverse and 0xC8 during Reverse; rare transitional values 0x48 and 0x88 also observed. Exact function not confirmed.";
